The compact/lsc argmin data above are still useful premises for proving
variational inequalities and uniqueness, but they are not by themselves a
compiled measurable-selection theorem.  This theorem is the active route:
prove continuity of the actual Eq. (4.4.56) selector, then measurability follows
by the standard Borel bridge. -/
theorem DualProxSelectorMeasurableAt_of_dual_selector_continuity
    (t : ℕ) (ht : 1 ≤ t)
    (hcont : setup.DualProxSelectorContinuousAt t ht) :
    setup.DualProxSelectorMeasurableAt t ht :=
  setup.DualProxSelectorMeasurableAt_of_continuous_selector t ht hcont

