/-- Core primal aggregate inequality for Lan Proposition 4.12 step 1.

Candidate audit: searched `two point aggregate average beta smooth convex hatf`
and `convex average beta weighted sum`. The finite Jensen helpers such as
`convexOn_weighted_average_le_weighted_sum` apply to normalized finite-window
averages, while this helper is the two-point APD recurrence using the midpoint
and output-average identities from Eq. (4.4.14)/(4.4.18). -/
private theorem deterministic_apd_hatf_aggregate_bound_core
    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [CompleteSpace E]
    {X : Set E} {f : E → ℝ} {grad xBarPrev xPrev xNext xBarNext xMid xTarget : E}
    {β L : ℝ}
    (hβ : 1 ≤ β)
    (hfconv : ConvexOn ℝ X f)
    (hxMid : xMid ∈ X) (hxBarPrev : xBarPrev ∈ X)
    (hxBarNext : xBarNext ∈ X) (hxTarget : xTarget ∈ X)
    (hgrad : HasGradientAt f grad xMid)
    (hsmooth :
      f xBarNext - f xMid - ⟪grad, xBarNext - xMid⟫_ℝ ≤
        (L / 2) * ‖xBarNext - xMid‖ ^ 2)
    (hbar_disp : xBarNext - xMid = β⁻¹ • (xNext - xPrev))
    (hmid_comb :
      (β - 1) • (xBarPrev - xMid) + (xTarget - xMid) = xTarget - xPrev) :
    β * f xBarNext - (β - 1) * f xBarPrev - f xTarget ≤
      ⟪grad, xNext - xTarget⟫_ℝ + (L / (2 * β)) * ‖xNext - xPrev‖ ^ 2 := by
  exact SOptLib.apd_primal_smooth_aggregate_bound
    (X := X) (f := f) (grad := grad)
    (xBarPrev := xBarPrev) (xPrev := xPrev) (xNext := xNext)
    (xBarNext := xBarNext) (xMid := xMid) (xTarget := xTarget)
    (β := β) (L := L)
    hβ hfconv hxMid hxBarPrev hxTarget (by
      simpa [InnerProductSpace.toDual_apply_eq_toDualMap_apply,
        InnerProductSpace.toContinuousLinearMap_toDualMap] using hgrad.hasFDerivAt)
    hsmooth hbar_disp hmid_comb

/-- Primal `\hat f` aggregate contribution in Lan Proposition 4.12 step 1.

Candidate audit: the reusable SOptLib smoothness candidates were checked, but
the setup already stores Lan Eq. (4.4.2) as `setup.hatf_smooth`; the finite
